1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:06,530 --> 00:00:09,810
So this fissure was left by your training.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:16,050
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

5
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:18,470
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

6
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:21,390
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

7
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:23,020
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

8
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:25,350
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

9
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:27,690
<i>Across this land</i>

10
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:30,020
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

11
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,480
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

12
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:44,790
<i>The story ends</i>

13
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:47,290
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

14
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:50,130
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

15
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:51,800
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

16
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:54,300
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

17
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,470
<i>Makes people forget</i>

18
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,260
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

19
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,060
<i>Begin to rust</i>

20
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,890
<i>Just the same</i>

21
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:05,180
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

22
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:08,520
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

23
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,400
<i>And they live on</i>

24
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:12,940
<i>We chose the same path</i>

25
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,070
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

26
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:16,610
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

27
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:20,870
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

28
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:22,240
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

29
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,330
<i>Even now</i>

30
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:25,700
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

31
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:29,250
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

32
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:30,920
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

33
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:56,410
You don't intend to fight
the dragon, do you?

34
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,590
So why do you continue training?

35
00:02:01,050 --> 00:02:03,160
When I arrived here,

36
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:07,560
all the villagers wore grim expressions
and lived in fear of the dragon.

37
00:02:08,490 --> 00:02:13,190
Now those same people are smiling happily.

38
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:17,290
They say this village is safe
because I'm around,

39
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:20,310
even though I haven't done anything.

40
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:25,670
The dragon simply hasn't attacked this
village because it doesn't feel like it.

41
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:35,820
If the dragon attacks the village,
will you fight it?

42
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,780
I don't want to die.

43
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:43,700
But to the people of this village,
I'm a hero.

44
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:47,140
I'm Stark, the hero of this village.

45
00:02:47,810 --> 00:02:49,880
I have to defend it.

46
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:56,710
That said, maybe I'd actually run away.

47
00:03:00,230 --> 00:03:06,800
I got this scar on my forehead during a
fight with my master, not against monsters.

48
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,230
That was the first time he ever hit me.

49
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,330
He must've been disappointed in me.

50
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:24,460
In the end, he never praised me. Not once.

51
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:33,510
What?

52
00:03:35,030 --> 00:03:38,820
I don't think you'll run.

53
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:43,080
You think you know me?

54
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:47,980
I don't know the first thing about you, but
I recalled my own terrifying experience.

55
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,600
A terrifying experience?

56
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,690
My first battle against a monster.

57
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,650
I'd trained plenty until then.

58
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:02,830
But my fear made me weak in the knees,

59
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:05,500
and I ran.

60
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:09,360
The monster wouldn't stop chasing me.

61
00:04:09,810 --> 00:04:12,490
For some reason, Ms. Frieren
wouldn't help me.

62
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:15,570
My master was like that, too.

63
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:17,420
When it finally cornered me

64
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,750
and I steeled my resolve,

65
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:22,090
my body moved.

66
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:30,000
All I needed was resolve.

67
00:04:30,690 --> 00:04:34,350
All the training you've done
won't let you down.

68
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:44,160
Though you're a hopeless coward, I believe
your resolve to protect the village is real.

69
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:55,170
Resolve, huh?

70
00:05:02,250 --> 00:05:03,370
How did it go?

71
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,510
I don't know.

72
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:08,970
I don't know,

73
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:13,370
but I think it'll be all right.

74
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,680
He's not here.

75
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:25,810
I guess he ran.

76
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:28,250
It's a shame. I had high hopes for him.

77
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,790
We have no choice.

78
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:32,570
Fern, we're going to play tag
with the dragon.

79
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:33,110
What?

80
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:37,890
Frieren.

81
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:42,590
You need me to keep it busy
for thirty seconds, right?

82
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,510
You're late.

83
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,630
Will you promise me one thing?

84
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:52,990
If I die during the battle,
I want you to finish off the dragon.

85
00:05:53,730 --> 00:05:56,220
Very well. I promise.

86
00:05:56,840 --> 00:06:00,850
But why are you willing to go
that far for the villagers?

87
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:04,650
What?

88
00:06:04,650 --> 00:06:07,720
I just thought it was a strange question.

89
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:11,240
I've lived in this village for three years.

90
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,090
That's not very long.

91
00:06:15,090 --> 00:06:16,120
Like heck it isn't.

92
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,220
Okay. Let's do this.

93
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:25,550
Your hands are trembling.

94
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:27,800
I'm afraid, after all.

95
00:06:29,610 --> 00:06:31,500
You don't have to laugh.

96
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,880
You're just like Eisen.

97
00:06:34,510 --> 00:06:35,890
My master?

98
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:39,230
Now this is a powerful foe.

99
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:43,380
Eisen, your hands are shaking.
Are you scared?

100
00:06:44,390 --> 00:06:45,400
Yeah.

101
00:06:45,890 --> 00:06:47,850
You'd admit it, just like that?

102
00:06:48,590 --> 00:06:51,670
Being afraid isn't a bad thing.

103
00:06:52,550 --> 00:06:57,510
It's my fear that brought me this far.

104
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,870
You even tremble the same way.

105
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,610
<i>I see.</i>

106
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:18,330
<i>My master was afraid, too.</i>

107
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:23,190
<i>All I need is resolve.</i>

108
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:28,960
He's entered the dragon's range.

109
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,900
It's not attacking.

110
00:07:32,970 --> 00:07:34,670
It's being cautious.

111
00:07:35,770 --> 00:07:37,250
I thought so.

112
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:48,410
No wonder it stopped attacking the village.

113
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,260
The dragon is a smart creature.

114
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:55,660
It's not stupid enough to pick a fight
against a powerful opponent.

115
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:00,180
Eisen didn't hit Stark for being weak,

116
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:05,590
or because he was disappointed in him.

117
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:13,560
<i>We parted in anger.</i>

118
00:08:14,310 --> 00:08:15,500
You hit him?

119
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:22,290
My body moved on reflex.

120
00:08:22,890 --> 00:08:25,480
I'm sorry for what I did to him.

121
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,660
I was afraid.

122
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:33,310
I was afraid of him, Frieren.

123
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:37,170
I couldn't believe it.

124
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:43,640
<i>My student will become
an incredible warrior.</i>

125
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,470
Now! Fire!

126
00:09:23,150 --> 00:09:25,620
Hey, why aren't you shooting at it?

127
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:27,610
I did exactly what you told me to do!

128
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:29,780
You expect me to fight it myself?

129
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,850
You can't be serious, you old hag!

130
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:33,920
You're just like my master after all!

131
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,660
It's already dead.

132
00:09:35,390 --> 00:09:36,250
What?

133
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,020
An old hag, huh?

134
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:41,910
<i>I'm scared of what she'll do later.</i>

135
00:09:45,370 --> 00:09:48,890
<i>I... killed it?</i>

136
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:54,570
<i>I defeated the dragon by myself?</i>

137
00:09:56,410 --> 00:09:57,590
Stark.

138
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:00,110
You did well.

139
00:10:00,440 --> 00:10:03,420
You exceeded my expectations. Well done.

140
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:09,110
Look at this mountain of treasure. Yippee!

141
00:10:09,110 --> 00:10:11,310
We can't take it all with us.

142
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,240
No more than three items.

143
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:24,320
This is ridiculous.

144
00:10:24,690 --> 00:10:26,940
You're interested in this stuff?

145
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:28,460
This stuff is a mountain of treasure.

146
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:35,170
My master said that you made the
heroes' adventure ridiculous.

147
00:10:35,590 --> 00:10:36,580
Oh?

148
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:41,250
He said it was a ridiculous and fun journey.

149
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:48,880
Wow, you actually made shaved ice!

150
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:51,810
I told you it was worth searching for.

151
00:10:51,810 --> 00:10:55,050
Not only that, but it's
fluffy instead of icy!

152
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:56,070
You're right.

153
00:10:56,070 --> 00:11:00,040
This is ridiculous. Should we
be wasting time on this?

154
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:04,440
Why not? Our journey's only just begun.

155
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:08,720
The Hero of the South, said to be
humanity's strongest fighter,

156
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:11,430
was defeated by the Demon King's
Seven Sages of Destruction.

157
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:17,290
We don't know if we'll make it back alive.

158
00:11:18,090 --> 00:11:21,670
Eisen, would you prefer a
difficult and painful journey?

159
00:11:24,930 --> 00:11:32,940
I'd rather enjoy a ridiculous and fun
journey I can laugh about when it's over.

160
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:39,560
Look! It melts as soon as you touch it!

161
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:41,310
Don't touch it. We're going to eat that.

162
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:42,330
Ridiculous.

163
00:11:42,330 --> 00:11:45,220
By the way, Frieren, what about syrup?

164
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,400
I don't have a spell to produce syrup.

165
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,250
You don't?

166
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:50,270
Truly ridiculous.

167
00:12:05,050 --> 00:12:07,730
Well? Can you see through them?

168
00:12:07,730 --> 00:12:12,090
Yes, but it's not a very interesting spell.

169
00:12:12,090 --> 00:12:15,050
Sorry my body's not more interesting.

170
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:18,880
What?

171
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:20,710
So small.

172
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,470
I'm not small!

173
00:12:22,930 --> 00:12:26,730
So, Stark, what will you do now?

174
00:12:26,730 --> 00:12:29,500
You can go back to Eisen, you know.

175
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:32,990
My master told you to take me
with you, didn't he?

176
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:34,690
Besides...

177
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:39,730
I feel like going on a
ridiculous journey, too.

178
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:54,530
Monsters are active in the northern lands.

179
00:12:55,010 --> 00:12:58,610
No one's allowed to pass through
the checkpoint currently.

180
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:02,850
When will the checkpoint open again?

181
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,430
Dunno.

182
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:07,380
At the very least, we've let none
through since I was posted here,

183
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:11,030
monsters and people alike.

184
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,610
Excuse me.

185
00:13:14,370 --> 00:13:17,020
Sir, the castellan would like to see you.

186
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:18,220
I'll be right there.

187
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:21,270
Listen here, adventurers.

188
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:25,330
Don't cause any trouble in this town.

189
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,860
That wasn't a very warm welcome.

190
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:36,900
You're right. He's a good guard.

191
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,730
Harsh on outsiders,

192
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:42,090
as town guards should be.

193
00:13:45,550 --> 00:13:50,120
Anyway, this city seems safe.

194
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,330
We'll wait here for a while.

195
00:13:53,450 --> 00:13:56,720
It'll be a good opportunity
to take our time studying magic.

196
00:13:56,720 --> 00:14:00,060
Once we drop our things off at the inn,
I'm going to the magic shops.

197
00:14:03,610 --> 00:14:07,850
What? The checkpoint's closed.
It's not like we have a choice.

198
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:10,670
Go on. You're free to go.

199
00:14:10,670 --> 00:14:12,700
I'm going to get us a room at the inn.

200
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,930
Wanna get something to eat?

201
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:20,430
Right. I'll go by myself.

202
00:14:21,690 --> 00:14:22,920
Scary...

203
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:30,980
I heard the sea routes have
been shut down recently, too.

204
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:35,050
The northern lands' army
plans to defeat them,

205
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:38,490
but it'll be at least two years
until the checkpoint opens.

206
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:41,350
Business is at a standstill.

207
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:46,380
I haven't had this in forever.

208
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:48,760
The jumbo-berry special.

209
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:53,100
I was just a kid when I came here before,
so I could hardly finish it.

210
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,150
I had to split it with my master.

211
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:59,340
I don't remember it being
this small, though.

212
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:03,980
It seems that way because
you're all grown up now.

213
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:09,000
I see. I've gotten bigger, huh?

214
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:12,810
Everything seemed so big when I was a kid.

215
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:16,600
Even my master's back that
once looked so broad

216
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,940
started looking small at some point.

217
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,970
Eisen's getting up there in age.

218
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:25,410
I hope you're being a dutiful student.

219
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:29,100
That's what I'm doing right now.

220
00:15:30,150 --> 00:15:32,400
Really, though, was it always <i>this</i> small?

221
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:35,800
The passage of time is cruel.

222
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:42,770
What? Got a problem?

223
00:15:42,770 --> 00:15:44,550
I bought it with my own money.

224
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:47,660
Excuse me. Could I get a glass of milk?

225
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:48,840
Sure thing.

226
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:54,060
What? Why are you mad?

227
00:15:55,110 --> 00:15:56,320
Mr. Stark.

228
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,540
Fine. You can have half.

229
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,200
That's not what I was going to say.

230
00:16:00,970 --> 00:16:05,870
What if I told you we might have to
wait more than two years in this city?

231
00:16:05,870 --> 00:16:07,350
What? No, thanks.

232
00:16:07,350 --> 00:16:09,850
Right? I don't want to, either.

233
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:11,020
Uh, yeah.

234
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:12,220
<i>What's her deal?</i>

235
00:16:12,530 --> 00:16:16,790
I'm relieved. You're normal.

236
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:19,720
Hey, did I do something to offend you?

237
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:24,370
A way through the checkpoint?

238
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:27,550
Sure, I'll help you look for one.

239
00:16:27,550 --> 00:16:29,360
Thank you.

240
00:16:29,910 --> 00:16:33,370
Would it be possible to fly over it?

241
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,550
The border with the northern lands

242
00:16:36,550 --> 00:16:39,650
is protected by a powerful barrier that
extends to maximum flying altitude.

243
00:16:39,650 --> 00:16:41,610
It can't be crossed.

244
00:16:41,610 --> 00:16:45,790
That makes sense. Otherwise flying
monsters would get right through.

245
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:50,360
Then we have no choice.
We'll hit up the merchants' guild.

246
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,500
They might at least be trading.

247
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,640
Trade has been shut down completely.

248
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:09,930
If guarded caravans aren't allowed through,

249
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:12,750
then the northern lands
must be quite dangerous.

250
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:16,760
We'll have to wait until
the situation settles down.

251
00:17:17,890 --> 00:17:22,390
No, let's hit up the black market
and thieves' guild first.

252
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:25,690
Isn't that a bit dangerous?

253
00:17:25,690 --> 00:17:31,000
We'll be fine. People think I look pretty
strong, and I'm a decent bluffer.

254
00:17:32,170 --> 00:17:33,910
And you've got the face of a scoundrel.

255
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:34,860
Shut up.

256
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:54,740
Well, that didn't work.

257
00:17:55,560 --> 00:18:00,010
I shouldn't be surprised. They're
basically fighting a defensive battle.

258
00:18:00,010 --> 00:18:02,320
There's nothing we can do
if the gates won't open.

259
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:06,880
Well, we've got nothing to lose.
Let's visit the guard station next.

260
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:10,850
What?

261
00:18:10,850 --> 00:18:15,530
I was just thinking you're being
especially cooperative.

262
00:18:15,530 --> 00:18:17,930
This was your idea.

263
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,090
I thought you didn't want to wait.

264
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:23,100
You seem more desperate than me.

265
00:18:25,650 --> 00:18:28,960
Well, I don't have a lot of time.

266
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:31,020
What do you mean?

267
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,970
The view from here is nice, isn't it?

268
00:18:35,970 --> 00:18:37,850
You can see the north side clearly.

269
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:42,240
When I was little,
my master brought me here.

270
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:50,050
We departed for the
northern lands from this city.

271
00:18:50,510 --> 00:18:52,640
What was your journey like, Master?

272
00:18:53,350 --> 00:18:57,990
You wanna know? Back then, we...

273
00:18:57,990 --> 00:19:01,130
Normally he hardly spoke about himself,

274
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,840
but he happily told me about
the heroes' adventure.

275
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:08,510
Across his long life,

276
00:19:08,510 --> 00:19:13,030
nothing was more important to him
than that ten-year adventure.

277
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,760
I'm sure the same is true for Frieren.

278
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,570
I wonder.

279
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:24,450
But he's too old to travel now.

280
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:29,200
And he told you to take me with you.

281
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:37,830
So I need to experience lots of
ridiculous and fun adventures in his place

282
00:19:37,830 --> 00:19:40,960
and bring back stories to tell him.

283
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:45,160
It's all I can do to repay my debt to him.

284
00:19:46,570 --> 00:19:50,300
If I take too long, my master will die.

285
00:19:53,530 --> 00:19:57,430
Then we can't allow ourselves
to be stopped here.

286
00:19:57,950 --> 00:20:02,080
I bet he's still got plenty
of years left, though.

287
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:19,710
Ms. Frieren, what are you doing here?

288
00:20:19,710 --> 00:20:21,630
Quiet.

289
00:20:22,190 --> 00:20:23,660
I'm being pursued.

290
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:34,470
Wh-What did you even do?

291
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:35,830
I don't know.

292
00:20:35,830 --> 00:20:38,640
I was just visiting various
magic shops, and then...

293
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:45,890
I'm sorry, Ms. Frieren!

294
00:20:45,890 --> 00:20:47,310
Please forgive me!

295
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:52,620
Wait. I don't like where this is going.

296
00:20:53,790 --> 00:20:57,660
It seems the guard captain was rude to you.

297
00:20:58,150 --> 00:21:01,920
As the castellan of this city,
I offer my apologies.

298
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:07,420
It doesn't bother me. He was
just doing his job as a guard.

299
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,620
I'm actually not in any kind of hurry.
I'm taking my time—

300
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:13,990
You plan to travel north again, don't you?

301
00:21:15,130 --> 00:21:18,950
I hear the northern lands are currently
engaged in an endless conflict

302
00:21:18,950 --> 00:21:21,050
with the remnants of the Demon King's forces.

303
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:24,200
You must be concerned about
the present situation.

304
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:27,950
Truly, you have the kindness of a hero.

305
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:32,040
The people of the northern lands
will be delighted as well.

306
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,460
Please feel free to pass
through the checkpoint.

307
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,220
I can't believe we're getting
through this easily.

308
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:55,300
Shouldn't we have told them
who you were from the start?

309
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:58,620
I didn't think there was any point.

310
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:01,220
I wanted to take my time, anyway.

311
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:05,320
And I don't really like this kind of thing.

312
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:08,510
It's an unsettling sight.

313
00:22:09,330 --> 00:22:12,120
I'm glad I got to see it, though.

314
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:23,620
This must be how my master
departed for the north, too.

315
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:37,520
You're right.

316
00:22:38,970 --> 00:22:43,360
Aw, darn. I wanted to do
more magical research.

317
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:44,680
You're still saying that?

318
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:48,360
We went through a lot of trouble
after that, you know. Right?

319
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:49,170
Yes.

320
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:52,520
<i>And you alright</i>

321
00:22:53,050 --> 00:22:55,040
<i>Can you hear me</i>

322
00:22:55,830 --> 00:23:01,940
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

323
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,270
<i>Crying excessively</i>

324
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:07,440
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

325
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:13,480
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

326
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:17,170
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

327
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:19,960
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

328
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:25,630
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

329
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:29,150
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

330
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:32,200
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

331
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,960
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

332
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:43,060
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

333
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:48,880
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

334
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:54,890
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

335
00:23:54,890 --> 00:24:00,650
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

336
00:24:00,650 --> 00:24:03,600
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

337
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,520
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

338
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:12,720
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

339
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:15,360
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

340
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:19,280
<i>for you to come back home</i>

341
00:24:20,390 --> 00:24:21,800
It hurts...

342
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:22,540
Humans love to make a fuss.

343
00:24:20,790 --> 00:24:23,510
He died in battle against
Aura ten years ago.

344
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:22,550
Mom...

345
00:24:22,550 --> 00:24:25,670
The Liberation Festival is tonight.

346
00:24:24,340 --> 00:24:26,310
Then we'd be no different from the demons.

347
00:24:24,570 --> 00:24:25,930
They're capable of speech.

348
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:27,810
I'm curious about that mage.

349
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,790
What a pain in the rear...

350
00:24:27,810 --> 00:24:29,870
It's like a fairy tale.
